================================================================================ PART 2: UNDERSTANDING HTML FORMS
What is a Form?

A form is:

• Collection of input fields - Text boxes, checkboxes, dropdowns, etc. • User interface for input - Way for users to provide information • Data collection mechanism - Gathers user-entered data • Submission mechanism - Sends data to server or processes locally • Validation mechanism - Checks data before submission • Interactive element - Responds to user actions • Structured data - Organizes information in predictable way • Communication tool - Enables user-to-app communication

Form Elements Overview

Here are the main form elements:

• Text Input - Single line text entry • Textarea - Multi-line text entry • Select/Dropdown - Choose from predefined options • Checkbox - Multiple selections allowed • Radio Button - Single selection from group • Button - Trigger actions (submit, reset, custom) • Label - Describes form fields • Form - Container for all form elements

