How Traditional Forms Work

The process is:

User fills form - Enters data into fields
User clicks submit - Triggers form submission
Browser collects data - Gathers all form field values
Browser sends request - Sends data to server (action URL)
Server processes - Backend processes the data
Server responds - Returns response (new page or confirmation)
Page reloads - Browser displays new page
Traditional Form Flow Diagram

Here's the flow:

User fills form ↓ User clicks submit button ↓ Browser collects form data ↓ Browser sends POST request to action URL ↓ Server receives data ↓ Server processes data ↓ Server sends response ↓ Browser loads new page

