================================================================================ PART 4: FORMS IN REACT
How Forms Work in React

In React, forms work differently:

• React manages form state - State tracks input values • Controlled components - React controls input values • Event handlers - Handle input changes and submission • No page reload - React updates UI without reload • Flexible validation - Can validate in real-time • Better UX - Immediate feedback to user • More control - React has full control over form

React Form Workflow

Here's how React forms work:

User types in input - Input value changes
onChange event fires - Event handler triggered
Handler updates state - setState called with new value
Component re-renders - React re-renders with new state
Input displays new value - User sees their input
User submits form - Clicks submit button
onSubmit event fires - Form submission handler triggered
Handler processes data - Can validate, send to server, etc.
No page reload - React handles everything
React Form Flow Diagram

Here's the flow:

User types in input ↓ onChange event fires ↓ Handler updates state (setState) ↓ Component re-renders ↓ Input displays new value ↓ User clicks submit ↓ onSubmit event fires ↓ Handler processes data ↓ No page reload - React handles it

