================================================================================ PART 7: FORM VALIDATION
Validation Techniques

Common validation techniques:

• Required fields - Check if field is not empty • Email validation - Check if email format is valid • Length validation - Check minimum/maximum length • Pattern validation - Check against regex pattern • Numeric validation - Check if value is number • Custom validation - Custom business logic • Real-time validation - Validate as user types • On-blur validation - Validate when field loses focus • On-submit validation - Validate when form submitted

Validation Example

Here's a validation function:

const validateForm = () => { const newErrors = {}

// Required field validation if (!formData.name.trim()) { newErrors.name = 'Name is required' }

// Email validation if (!formData.email.trim()) { newErrors.email = 'Email is required' } else if (!formData.email.includes('@')) { newErrors.email = 'Email must be valid' }

// Length validation if (formData.password.length < 8) { newErrors.password = 'Password must be at least 8 characters' }

// Pattern validation (phone number) const phoneRegex = /^\d{10}$/ if (!phoneRegex.test(formData.phone)) { newErrors.phone = 'Phone must be 10 digits' }

// Numeric validation if (isNaN(formData.age) || formData.age < 18) { newErrors.age = 'Age must be 18 or older' }

// Custom validation if (formData.password === formData.username) { newErrors.password = 'Password cannot be same as username' }

return newErrors }

